	(text "Photodiode Amplifier Circuit"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 247.65 261.62 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "f75fa92d-95d2-42c3-86f3-214b36dfb097")
	)
	(text "Math for passive component values:\n\n1. Select the gain resistor.\n	R1 = (V_{oMax} − V_{oMin}) / I_{iMax} \n	= (4.9V − 0.1V) / 27μA = 177.8kΩ ≈ 174kΩ (Standard Value)\n2. Select the feedback capacitor to meet the circuit bandwidth.\n	C1 ≤ 1 / (2π x R1 x f_{p})\n	C1 ≤ 1 / (2π x 174kΩ x 20kHz)) \n	≤ 45.7pF ≈ 39pF (C0G/NP0) (Standard Value)\n3. Calculate the op amp gain bandwidth (GBW) for the circuit to be stable.\n	GBW > (C_{i} + C_{1}) / (2π × R1 × C1^{2}) \n	> ((12.3pF + 39pF) / (2π × 174kΩ × (39pF)^{2})) = 31kHz\n	where C_{i} = C_{j} + C_{d} + C_{cm} = 3.3pF + 2.5pF + 6.5pF = 12.3pF given\n	• C_{j}: Junction capacitance of photodiode\n	• C_{d}: Differential input capacitance of the amplifier\n	• C_{cm}: Common-mode input capacitance of the inverting input\n	GBW_{OPA2350} = 38MHz\n4. Calculate the bias network for a 0.1V bias voltage.\n	R2 = ((Vcc − Vref) / Vref) × R3\n	R2 = ((5V − 0.1V) / 0.1V) × R3\n	R2 = 49 × R3\n	Closest 1% resistor values that yield this relationship are\n	R2 = 49.9kΩ and R3 = 1kΩ\n5. Select C2 to be 1μF to filter the Vref voltage. \n	The resulting cutoff frequency is:\n	f_{p} = 1 / (2π × C2 × R2 ∥ R3) \n	= 1 / (2π × 1μF × 50k ∥ 1k) \n	≈ 159Hz"
		(exclude_from_sim yes)
		(at 267.462 217.424 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.524 1.524)
				(thickness 0.1588)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "f7a5f6f7-ad22-4587-9f89-1dcf224cefe9")
	)
